[2026-11-27T11:58:51Z] note: answers: user chose (2026-11-27) to run the pair specs with a labelled assumed borrow fee on the short leg (0.25 %/yr base for easy-to-borrow ETFs/large caps, stress 1 % and 3 %) instead of disabling them as the spec requires without borrow data.
[2026-11-27T11:58:52Z] note: assumptions: AR(1) fit and z-score both on the prior n bars; half-life lower bound 2 and entry z -2 / stop z -4 are fixed constants. | BORROW COST ASSUMED (user decision 2026-11-27): the spec says to disable pairs without historical borrow/carry data; there is none, so the short leg pays a constant labelled fee (CONFIG borrow_fee_pct_yr: 0.25 %/yr for these easy-to-borrow ETFs/large caps, 3 %/yr for crypto margin) on its market value per calendar day; stress runs at higher fees are logged after the optimization. Borrow recalls and margin calls are not modelled. | short proceeds earn 0 % and the long leg is paid from the sleeve (no margin interest): conservative carry; total-return (adjusted) closes on both legs, so the short leg pays the dividends it is short (dividend-in-lieu). | gross notional G = 100 % of sleeve equity at entry (equal dollars: G/2 each; ratio 1:beta: long G/(1+beta), short beta*G/(1+beta)); quantities frozen at entry. | same-bar ambiguity: if a leg's stop is touched intrabar, that leg fills at its stop and the other leg at its worst bar extreme (long: low, short: high); if both legs touch, the long leg is assumed first. Gaps through a stop fill both legs at the open. | no new entry on a bar where a position was closed, and no entry when the exit condition (or a forced window end) is true on the signal bar. | costs: library convention (ETFs fee 0.05 % + slippage 0.03 % per fill; crypto 0.10 % + 0.10 %), both legs, entry and exit. | IAU, EWA, EWC and VDE were not in the project; their Yahoo daily history was fetched on 2026-11-27 (src.collectors.yahoo_daily.update, full history) without adding them to config/symbols.yaml, so the nightly job doesn't refresh them.
[2026-11-27T11:58:52Z] note: backtest.py adapted from template: built by scripts/portfolio_lib/build_pairs.py = this spec's signals() + shared pair simulator pair_core.py (EXECUTION.md pair execution: synchronized next-open fills, per-leg hard stops, close-based pair stop, max_candles, entry veto, borrow accrual) + panel/indicators from core.py + the template's generic machinery; run() simulates one pair.
[2026-11-27T11:58:52Z] note: sanity check: spec defaults IS: 39 trades, -1.72 %/yr, max DD -34.63 % (OOS 22 trades, -1.38 %/yr, DD -16.45 %). Verified on generated trades (ratio_zscore, normalized_distance, ratio_rsi): every entry follows an entry signal on the previous bar with no exit signal; signal exits follow an exit signal; after an exit no fill on the same bar (e.g. KO/PEP stopped 2008-07-01, next entry 2008-07-03); sum of trade P&L = equity change (-769.93 over 'all'); borrow fee lowers results monotonically (0 / 0.25 / 3 %/yr -> IS net 466 / 450 / 282). Engle-Granger p at MacKinnon's 5 % critical value (-3.34, N=2) = 0.0495.
